{title: Sons of Dishon}
{subtitle: Genesis 36:26; 36:20–21; 1 Chronicles 1:41; Deuteronomy 2:12–22}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The land of Seir held the old ways
The Horite chiefs kept the mountain days
Lotan and Shobal stood the test
Zibeon [F]and Anah were the best
[C]Dishon and Es[Dm]hban stood tall who lived in the land
Dis[F]han was the last of the [C]band
These were the [Dm]sons of Seir the Horite
In the place that they [Bb]called their site
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Hemdan and Eshban [Dm]stood tall
Ithran and [F]Keran heard the [C]call
Sons of Dishon in [Gm]the genealogy
[Dm]Names written in the [F]history
[C]Before the Esauites [Gm]took the land
They [Bb]walked across the Seir land
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The descendants of E[Dm]sau came near
They drove the old clans from the sphere
Wiped them out and settled in place
Just like Israel in that loca[F]tion
Thir-ty-eight years the [C]men did fade
[Dm]The hand of the Lord was in the shade
[F]To root them out until [C]they perished
[Dm]As the Lord had sworn and whispered
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Hem[Bb]dan and Eshban stood tall
[Dm]Ithran and Keran [F]heard the call
[C]Sons of Dishon in [Gm]the genealogy
[Dm]Names written in the his[F]tory
Be[C]fore the Esauites took the [Gm]land
They [Bb]walked across the Seir land
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Anah had a son named [Dm]Dishon [Bb][C][Dm][Bb][C][Dm]
His lineage is not forgotten
Cherans and Kerans keep the name
Though the power slowly changed
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
They lived [Bb]in Seir to this day [Dm]
Under the shadow of the sway
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Interlude}
